Custom sunnypilot Branch + SSH Installation Guide
1. Create Your Own sunnypilot Branch
Go to Official repo and Click: Fork

This creates:
  https://github.com/YOURNAME/sunnypilot

Clone your fork locally
  git clone https://github.com/YOURNAME/sunnypilot.git
  cd sunnypilot

Add official repo as upstream
  git remote add upstream https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot.git
  git fetch upstream

Create your custom branch from official release
  git checkout -b mazdafix upstream/release-mici

This creates:

  mazdafix

based on the latest official:

  release-mici
2. Apply Mazda Standstill Alert Fix
High-level change summary

The Mazda CX-5 2022+ allows LKAS steering at 0 mph (minSteerSpeed = 0).

During EPS startup at standstill:

Mazda EPS temporarily reports:
LKAS_BLOCK = True

Original sunnypilot logic incorrectly interpreted this as a steering fault, causing:

"Place Hands on Wheel"

alerts during stop-and-go traffic.

Fix concept

The patch:

adds an EPS initialization filter
waits until LKAS successfully initializes once
ignores temporary startup LKAS_BLOCK states
includes a timeout so real hardware faults are still detected

Only one file was modified:

opendbc_repo/opendbc/car/mazda/carstate.py
Apply patch
git apply mazda_fix.patch

Verify:

git diff

Commit:

git add .
git commit -m "Add Mazda standstill LKAS init fix"

Push branch:

git push origin mazdafix
3. SSH Installation on comma 4
Generate SSH Key on Windows

Open PowerShell:

  ssh-keygen -t ed25519

Press Enter through all prompts.

Default location:

  C:\Users\YOURNAME\.ssh\id_ed25519
Show Public Key
  cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

Copy the ENTIRE output line.

Example:

  ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1... USER@PC
Add SSH Key to GitHub

Go here:

GitHub SSH Keys

Click:

New SSH Key

Paste the public key.

Enable SSH Access on comma

On comma:

Settings → Developer → SSH Keys

Enter your GitHub username.

comma automatically downloads your public SSH keys from GitHub.

SSH Into comma

Find comma IP:

Settings → Network

Then from PowerShell:

ssh comma@192.168.X.XXX

Successful login looks like:

comma@tici:~$
4. Install Your Custom sunnypilot Branch
Backup existing install
cd /data
mv openpilot openpilot_backup
Clone your custom branch
git clone -b mazdafix --recurse-submodules https://github.com/YOURNAME/sunnypilot.git openpilot
Pull Git LFS files
cd openpilot
git lfs pull
Reboot comma
sudo reboot
5. Recovery (If Something Breaks)

SSH into comma again:

cd /data
rm -rf openpilot
mv openpilot_backup openpilot
sudo reboot
